{
  "vocabulary": "interests",
  "version": "1.1.0",
  "notes": [
    "Shared label set for KG MATCHES edges and LLM constraint extraction (coordinate changes with the conversation component owner).",
    "Labels are coarse recipient interests. Recipient types, occasions, age and budget belong to the conversation state and must not be added here.",
    "Confidence values are heuristic rule scores, not calibrated probabilities. An edge with several evidence items takes the max (no noisy-OR).",
    "Phrases are matched case-insensitively on whole words; a space also matches a hyphen. A match overlapping an 'exclude' phrase is discarded.",
    "Books: category rules plus a few explicit books_title_phrases only. Book features and all descriptions are never used for interests.",
    "Feature text only corroborates (feature_evidence = corroborating_only). An interest supported by feature phrases alone is an incidental mention and creates no MATCHES edge.",
    "text_suppression: in Handmade/Toys, products whose title head (text before the first separator or bracket) names a party/event supply or nursery/infant product get no title-, feature- or Theme-based interests. Their motif is decoration for an event or a baby's room, not the recipient's interest. Category rules still apply. For party_supplies, a phrase introduced by \"for\"/\"as\" (\"Coin Toys for Party Favor\") is a suggested use and does not count.",
    "details.Theme values listing more than theme_max_values comma-separated motifs are ignored.",
    "Each MATCHES edge carries match_type: primary (category rule, or a Books title phrase) or themed (motif, licensed character or design found in title/Theme)."
  ],
  "confidence": {
    "category": 0.9,
    "details_theme": 0.7,
    "title": 0.7,
    "title_books": 0.6,
    "features": 0.5
  },
